                <pb facs="1143" n="1063" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg1063"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hill to Mr. Bowen.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-04-25"><hi rendition="#italic">April 25,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hill states that the Government of the United States regards the course of
                    the Government of Venezuela respecting the steamer <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Viking</hi> as contrary to international law, and requests that the
                    Venezuelan consul be directed to issue clearance papers or that those of the
                    United States consul be respected, and that prompt action is required.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
